nczos (Wu–Simon) with full reorthogonalization and locking on −A, from a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fixed start vector; once k pairs are found, a run on the complement of their vectors checks","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that no copy of a multiple eigenvalue was missed. A Ritz pair is accepted when its residual","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is at most ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance"},{"text":" · max(|λ|, s\/1000), s Gershgorin’s bound on the spectrum; the vectors","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are then rotated by Rayleigh–Ritz on M, whose values are returned. The dense solver below 64","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices, or when k is a third of them or more.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"O((n + m) · products + n · k²) time, O(n · k) ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"text":"s for the vectors and n · max(30, 2k +","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"10) for the basis.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"weight","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" gives the weight of the edge at each position, read once per position.","type":"text"}]},{"name":"Precondition","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"smallest"},{"text":" is in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0...vertexCount"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance > 0"},{"text":", every weight is finite,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"text":", when given, is at least 1.","type":"text"}]}],"style":"note","type":"aside"},{"name":"Throws","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"code":"NoConvergence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when a Lanczos run spends ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" products without","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"converging, with the products spent and the largest Ritz residual on the tolerance’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"scale. The dense solver throws as ","type":"text"},{"code":"adjacencySpectrum","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" does.","type":"text"}]}],"style":"note","type":"aside"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/adjacencyEigenpairs(smallest:weight:tolerance:maxIterations:)-2ye38","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The k smallest eigenvalues of the adjacency matrix A ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"adjacencyMatrix()"},{"type":"text","text":"), k = "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"smallest"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ascending, each with a unit eigenvector (see "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Eigenpairs"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"references":{"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory/GraphProtocols/Graph/adjacencyEigenpairs(smallest:weight:tolerance:maxIterations:)-2ye38":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph\/adjacencyeigenpairs(smallest:weight:tolerance:maxiterations:)-2ye38","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The k smallest eigenvalues of the adjacency matrix A ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"adjacencyMatrix()"},{"type":"text","text":"), k = "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"smallest"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"ascending, each with a unit eigenvector (see ","type":"text"},{"code":"Eigenpairs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"adjacencyEigenpairs"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"